<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Opportunity.object-meta.xml - build northwind-sales, step M3-S05.

  This file exists for one reason: a FlexiPage carries no assignment. The full field list of
  the FlexiPage type is description, events, flexiPageRegions, masterLabel, pageTemplate,
  parentFlexiPage, platformActionlist, quickActionList, sobjectType, template, type - eleven
  fields, "none of them an audience"
  (skills/admin/lightning-record-page-configuration/references/gotchas.md Gotcha 1). Ship the
  flexipages folder alone and the deploy is green while every user still sees the old page.

  The org default (Rung 3) lives here, in an ActionOverride whose actionName is View, type is
  Flexipage, content is the page name and formFactor selects the environment. Block shape and
  element order copied verbatim from
  skills/admin/lightning-record-page-configuration/references/examples.md Example 1 Step 2.

  Two blocks, not one. formFactor is a field on the override, not on the page: "Large is the
  Lightning Experience desktop environment, Small is the Salesforce mobile app, and an absent
  or null formFactor means Salesforce Classic. Three different values, three independent
  assignments, one page... covering both is literally two overrides that differ in one
  element" (gotchas.md Gotcha 3, quoting the ActionOverride reference). Assumption A17 puts
  this build on Lightning Experience desktop AND the Salesforce mobile app, and the M3-S04
  bundle declares supportedFormFactors Large and Small to match, so dropping the Small block
  would leave mobile reps on whatever the next rung supplies. Note that the only fenced
  OBJECT-file example in the library shows Large alone; the pair is fenced at app level
  (gotchas.md Gotcha 3, the Dreamhouse sample). The element set is identical in both, and the
  formFactor semantics quoted above are stated against ActionOverride - the object-level type.

  Why this file ships on M3-S05 and not on the object-model step M1-S01: plan decision D10.
  check_lightning_record_page_configuration.py reads objects/*/*.object-meta.xml relative to
  its manifest-dir argument and does not recurse, so the page and its override must sit in one step
  directory or the assignment check cannot run at all. No path collision: M1-S01 writes the
  decomposed recordTypes, businessProcesses and fields files and no Opportunity.object-meta.xml.

  This file carries actionOverrides and nothing else. It is a partial standard-object file:
  deploying it adds the two overrides and changes no other Opportunity configuration.
-->
<CustomObject xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <actionOverrides>
        <actionName>View</actionName>
        <content>Opportunity_Enterprise_Record_Page</content>
        <formFactor>Large</formFactor>
        <type>Flexipage</type>
    </actionOverrides>
    <actionOverrides>
        <actionName>View</actionName>
        <content>Opportunity_Enterprise_Record_Page</content>
        <formFactor>Small</formFactor>
        <type>Flexipage</type>
    </actionOverrides>
</CustomObject>
